{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792308781,"nonce":"KzlAPq9t12x2P4qnFp3yIBJjXTE=","title":"CodeEditor: a minimap that also navigates the code","message":"Requested by the RayDE session, for the user; RayDE's tracker has it as bb19773 (editor extension points), beside ashui's 495aa31. Modelled on VS Code.\n\n**What is wanted**\n\n- A narrow strip down the editor's right edge that draws the whole document scaled down: one thin row per line, each token a coloured run in its syntax colour. Block mode is enough; the characters need not be legible.\n- A prop turns it on, `minimap`, off by default so CodeView and other users stay as they are, with a maximum width and a choice of characters or blocks.\n- A viewport slider over the strip marks the part of the document on screen, and follows scrolling.\n- Navigation: clicking the strip scrolls the editor to that line; dragging the slider scrolls as it is dragged; the wheel over the strip scrolls the editor. The strip reads `scroll` and writes it back.\n- A document whose scaled height is more than the editor's makes the strip scroll proportionally, as VS Code's does.\n- Folded lines are skipped (`document.visible`), so the strip matches what the editor shows.\n- Cheap: rows cached per revision, only the slider redrawn on scroll, and a canvas draw or one texture rather than an element per line. RayDE opens files of thousands of lines.\n- Markers are for later, tied to the decorations of 495aa31: the selection, search matches and diagnostics, errors and warnings in their own colours, should be able to paint into it.\n- Styled by tokens like the rest of ashui: `--ui-code-minimap-bg`, `--ui-code-minimap-slider` (idle and hover colours) and `--ui-code-minimap-border`; the slider has a hover state and a dragging state.","files":null}]}